    "q-136954": {
      "dom_id": "step-q136954",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ and vector $b$ shown above. If the general least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ is \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R,\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $2a+\\frac{b}{c}?$",
      "worked_solution": "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}\\,Ax={A}^{T}b\n$$\n\nNotice that the columns of $A$ are linearly dependent. So first, let's write down the normal equation in matrix form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}6 & -18 \\\\ -18 & 54\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system corresponding to the above matrix equation using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & -18 & -3 \\\\ -18 & 54 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}6 & -18 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{2}+3{x}_{2}.\n$$\n\n Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}+3{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$2a+\\frac{b}{c}=2\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})+\\frac{3}{1}=2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
