    "q-137086": {
      "dom_id": "step-q137086",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ {x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear equations shown above. If the general least-squares solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $12a+\\frac{b}{c}?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we write our system in matrix form as $Ax=b,$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}\\,Ax={A}^{T}b\n$$\n\nNotice that the columns of $A$ are linearly dependent. So first, let's write down the normal equation in matrix form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 6 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 6 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}6 & -18 \\\\ -18 & 54\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ 30\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system corresponding to the final matrix equation using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & -18 & -10 \\\\ -18 & 54 & 30\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}6 & -18 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-\\frac{5}{3}+3{x}_{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{3}+3{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n12a+\\frac{b}{c}=12\\cdot (-\\frac{5}{3})+\\frac{3}{1}=-17.\n$$",
